The paper’s native problem is exact edge editing to a \(P_4\)-free graph. Recognition of a submitted edited graph is polynomial, but finding an edit set is NP-hard and FPT in budget \(k\); the paper’s kernel specifically makes small fixed \(k\) an easy regime. I’m now checking the full proofs and quantitative regime before deciding between a native Track A family and a Track B construction.
